# Machine-specific overrides only. .claude/settings.json IS committed now: it
# registers the session-start hook, which is what gets a fresh web container
# to the point where it can lint, typecheck, build and run the suite. It was
# ignored on the assumption graphify would generate a machine-specific one --
# it does not; `graphify claude install` had written nothing but that same
# hook registration. Anything genuinely per-machine goes in settings.local.json.
.claude/settings.local.json

# machine-local graphify pointers and auto-backups (regenerated on any machine)
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root
graphify-out/20*/

# Graph artefacts that regenerate themselves.
#
# .github/workflows/graphify-deploy.yml rebuilds every project's graph from
# source on each push to main and republishes the HTML to Pages, and
# `graphify update` rebuilds it locally. Committing the output as well made
# the diffs unreadable -- 101,531 lines added and 45,119 deleted across nine
# commits, in files no human opens -- and dirtied the working tree merely by
# running a query.
#
# The semantic layer is deliberately NOT ignored: .graphify_labels.json,
# cache/semantic/ and cost.json are the output of an LLM pass that cost real
# money, and CI's --code-only rebuild cannot recreate them.
graphify-out/graph.json
graphify-out/graph.html
graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
graphify-out/manifest.json
graphify-out/cache/stat-index.json
graphify-out/cache/last_query_stamp
graphify-out/cache/ast/
*/graphify-out/graph.json
*/graphify-out/graph.html
*/graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
*/graphify-out/manifest.json
*/graphify-out/cache/stat-index.json
*/graphify-out/cache/last_query_stamp
*/graphify-out/cache/ast/
